D3D12: CmdClearAttachments works in a stencil-only pass.

CommandBufferD3D12::ClearAttachments takes the depth-stencil view from m_Depth.attachment, which
BeginRendering sets only from RenderingDesc::depth; a pass given only RenderingDesc::stencil has
m_Stencil.attachment and a null m_Depth.attachment, so the call dereferences null. Since 110a667.

This takes the view from the depth attachment, or else from the stencil one.
Measured on v190, NVIDIA: BeginRendering with a D32_SFLOAT_S8_UINT view as stencil only, then
CmdClearAttachments with planes = STENCIL, ended the process with an access violation (0xC0000005)
inside the call; Vulkan cleared. With the change, a stencil cleared to 5 by BeginRendering and to 7
by ClearAttachments in one quadrant makes a later EQUAL 7 draw cover exactly that quadrant, on both
backends, layers clean.

diff --git a/Source/D3D12/CommandBufferD3D12.hpp b/Source/D3D12/CommandBufferD3D12.hpp
index d635c0a..7a09498 100644
--- a/Source/D3D12/CommandBufferD3D12.hpp
+++ b/Source/D3D12/CommandBufferD3D12.hpp
@@ -1763,7 +1763,8 @@ NRI_INLINE void CommandBufferD3D12::ClearAttachments(const ClearAttachmentDesc*
             if (clearAttachmentDesc.planes & PlaneBits::STENCIL)
                 clearFlags |= D3D12_CLEAR_FLAG_STENCIL;
 
-            D3D12_CPU_DESCRIPTOR_HANDLE handle = {m_Depth.attachment->GetDescriptorHandleCPU()};
+            const DescriptorD3D12* depthStencil = m_Depth.attachment ? m_Depth.attachment : m_Stencil.attachment; // a stencil-only pass has no depth attachment
+            D3D12_CPU_DESCRIPTOR_HANDLE handle = {depthStencil->GetDescriptorHandleCPU()};
             GetGraphicsCommandList()->ClearDepthStencilView(handle, clearFlags, clearAttachmentDesc.value.depthStencil.depth, clearAttachmentDesc.value.depthStencil.stencil, rectNum, d3dRects);
         }
     }
